  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_0' aria-label=\" M/s Balaji Formalin Pvt. Ltd. & Anr. versus Union of India & Anr. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('0','2026','2026_10_232_258',''); ><font size='4'> <strong>M/S BALAJI FORMALIN PVT. LTD. & ANR.<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>UNION OF INDIA & ANR. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 10 S.C.R. 232</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010003372026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : K. VINOD CHANDRAN<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, J.B. PARDIWALA</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Issue arose whether rr.18A and 18B, inserted by the Maharashtra Poisons (Amendment) Rules, 2011, in the Maharashtra Poisons Rules, 1972, could be said to be violative of Arts.14 and 19(1)(g) of the Constitution. Headnotes&dagger; Maharashtra Poisons Rules, 1972 &ndash; Validity of &ndash; Writ petition by the petitioners seeking declaration that Notification dated 21.01.2011 be declared ultra vires the Poisons Act, 1919, as well as the Constitution to the extent of insertion of rr.18A and 18B, respectively in the Maharashtra Poisons Rules &ndash;<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 18-09-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> WRIT PETITION (CIVIL) No. 893/2019</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Disposed off</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('0','2026','2026_10_232_258','','S')><img src='images/split_24.svg' alt='' aria-hidden='true'>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class=